1 Upon request:

a. the mayor and aldermen shall grant everyone access to the basic register and shall provide everyone with the data included in the basic register;

b. the Service shall grant everyone access to the national facility and shall provide everyone with the data included in the national facility.

2 Article 10 of the Freedom of Information Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the inspection and provision of data referred to in the first paragraph, insofar as:

a. to the extent that an administrative body or other recipient is granted access to the basic register or the national facility using search services, only the grounds referred to in Article 10(1)(b), (2)(a) and (7)(b) of the Freedom of Information Act shall apply mutatis mutandis;

b. to the extent that an administrative body is granted access to the basic register or the national facility with a view to fulfilling a public law task that may have an impact on the environment using consultation services, or if data are provided to that administrative body from the address register or the building register or from the national facility with a view to fulfilling that task, only the grounds referred to in Article 10(1)(b), (2)(a) and (c) and (7)(b) of the Freedom of Information Act shall apply mutatis mutandis.

In its application to the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (hereinafter referred to as the "Organization"), the standard provisions shall be applicable with the following modifications:

1. Article V and paragraph 2 (I) of Article VII shall also apply to the President of the Council of the Organization, except that any waiver of the immunity of the President under paragraph 16 shall be effected by the Council of the Organization.

2. (i) Experts (other than officials coming within the scope of Article VI) serving as members of committees or as staff of the Organization shall be accorded the following privileges and immunities, to the extent necessary for the independent exercise of their functions, including the time spent in travelling in connection with the exercise of their functions in those committees or in the performance of their duties:

(a) immunity from personal arrest or detention and from search, provided that the immunity from immunity from personal arrest or detention and from search shall not apply to crimes committed against the life, physical integrity or health of others;

(b) immunity from legal process in respect of words spoken or written and acts done by them in their official capacity; this immunity shall continue to be accorded after they have ceased to hold office in the committees of the Organization or to perform their duties for the Organization;

(c) the same facilities as regards restrictions on the movement and use of funds and the conversion of funds as those accorded to officials of the Organization.
